## What this notice covers (2026-08-22 · last revised 2026-08-23 — D-103, D-104, D-112, D-113)

This file is the **retained upstream notice** for content borrowed from
`babamba2/superclaude-for-sap` (via the frozen `hjaewon/sc4sap-custom`).
It is **not the license of the SAPKIT plugin** — that is the repository root
`LICENSE` (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Hong Jaewon). Nothing above has been altered
and nothing above will be: this section only records what is known about the
subtree it covers.

**It covers the whole `interactive/` subtree.** Two attempts to narrow it to a
file list failed review (a migration class was missed, then the ledger's path
mapping was found short), and the re-authoring that followed showed why a file
list is the wrong shape: what remains of the upstream work is not files but
**scattered contract lines**. What is known today, ledger by ledger:

| Group | Count | State |
|---|---:|---|
| `server/sap-assets/` | 30 files | Upstream, unmodified since import. Kept as-is by D-079 ⑥ — these install SAP-side objects that are never renamed or regenerated. **Permanent, and the reason this notice never fully retires.** |
| Knowledge, industry, country and ABAP-convention content (`copy` ledger) | 170 files | **Re-authored file by file under independent review** (finished 2026-08-18) — except **26 pure reference-table files** (TCode/SPRO tables), which were **verified unchanged** instead: their content is factual data, kept byte-identical on purpose (D-088 ②). |
| Server-bound utilities and the tool catalog | 6 files | **Replaced or rewritten 2026-08-23**: the catalog is now generated from the engine registry; both utilities were rewritten from scratch. |
| Personas, procedures, hooks, libs, extraction tools, policies (§3.4 ledger) | 56 files | **Re-authored 2026-08-23** across three reviewed batches. |
| What still matches the upstream text | **~2,200 lines across ~130 files, outside `server/`** (~600/40 in the §3.4 ledger · ~950/64 in re-authored `copy` files · ~660/25 in the unchanged reference tables — 25 of the 26 show overlap at the 3-line cut) | **Contract lines and reference data, kept deliberately**: tables and TCode/identifier data, output templates and print-verbatim blocks, checklists (re-authoring of these is deferred, not judged done), user-facing trigger phrases and approval keywords, shared-block labels and paths. Almost all explanatory prose has been re-authored — a handful of byte-identical normative sentences remain and are itemized in the ledger. |

The accounting lives in `docs/reference/copy-baseline.md` (§3.4 — 56/56
checked); the plan and its end-state are `docs/BLUEPRINT.md`.
